# Copy to .env and fill in.

# Required. Server-side key for the food-parsing endpoint (api/parse-food.ts).
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-google-gemini-api-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, and only for upgrading an installation that previously used Supabase.
# Put these in frontend/.env. They let the one-time importer read a returning
# user's old cloud history. Safe to omit for a fresh install; delete them once
# the migration window has passed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_KEY=your-anon-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: Google Drive sync (frontend/.env).
# Client ID only — the browser token flow never uses the client secret, and a
# VITE_ variable is inlined into the public bundle, so a secret here is public.
# See docs/SYNC_SETUP.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=xxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server (Express API, server/). Required to start the server.
# DATABASE_URL: PostgreSQL connection string, e.g. from your Supabase project
#   (Connect → connection string). Keep the real value in .env only.
# JWT_SECRET: at least 32 random characters, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 48`.
# CORS_ORIGIN: the frontend origin allowed to call the API.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/postgres
# JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string-of-at-least-32-chars
# CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
# PORT=8787
